  "query_preview": "..Cold front comes through on Wednesday, but looks too\nstarved for moisture to produce any rain. Sharper northwest flow \naloft and stronger shortwave may drop across late this week, but\nstrongest lifts probably stays north resulting in LREF showing \nless than 25% chance of seeing even a few hundredths. Maybe a bit\nbetter shot of some rain beyond next weekend per LREF and AI \nguidance, but overall as mid shift said, the longer we go without\nsignificant rain, we could start to have increasing fire weather \nconcerns over the next several weeks due to current drought status\nand increasing fine fuels as we experience repeated frost/freeze\nconditions.",
